{"chunk_id": "1d3bfe9d84f6", "text": "These pages narrate the sacred marriage of Shiva and Parvati, highlighting divine ritual, cosmic symbolism, and tender moments between the couple. After Parvati\u2019s invitation reaches Kailasa, the gods prepare magnificently for the wedding. Shiva arrives at the Himalayan capital with celestial hosts and humbly bows at a shrine of Rama and Sita. The couple share a silent, powerful exchange of love before the ceremony. During the rite, Narada explains that Shiva has no lineage because he is the source of all creation, astonishing the assembly. The marriage is sealed with the tying of the mangala sutra and Vedic rites. Later scenes show playful affection at the wedding feast, Shiva restoring Manmatha to life, and philosophical teaching about the unity of the Trinity. The chapter closes with emotional farewells as Parvati leaves her parents for Kailasa.\nShiva and Parvati\u2019s divine wedding is celebrated with rituals, blessings, philosophical teachings, and a farewell as Parvati departs for Kailasa.\nThemes: divine marriage, ritual and tradition, devotion and humility, cosmic unity of Trinity, marital duty", "vector": [0.013405327685177326, -0.015168838202953339, 0.0019358831923455, 0.009500413201749325, -0.016813013702630997, 0.011781042441725731, -0.02069803886115551, -0.016706937924027443, -0.012868319638073444, -0.0351376049220562, -0.0013831289252266288, 0.03484589606523514, -0.009579969570040703, 0.0014684867346659303, -0.0008502637501806021, 0.016123520210385323, 0.04054747149348259, -0.03269786387681961, 0.02266044169664383, -0.024848254397511482, 0.00048107028123922646, 0.008731363341212273, -0.0004108365101274103, 0.013034062460064888, -0.0246493611484766, 0.008572249673306942, 0.0238935723900795, -0.019570983946323395, 0.002361843828111887, -0.013126878999173641, -0.021904651075601578, -0.010912546887993813, -0.010528022423386574, -0.03861158713698387, -0.010368908755481243, -0.015447286888957024, 0.0028607314452528